{"_v":1,"id":"woman-in-mind-west-end-2025","bd":{"positive":4,"mixed":5,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Claire Allfree","o":"The Telegraph","s":88,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/theatre/what-to-see/woman-in-mind-duke-of-yorks-theatre-review/","d":"2026-01-07","q":"Longhurst’s revival is correspondingly both a Middle England sitcom and a psychedelic fever dream."},{"cn":"Clive Davis","o":"The Times (UK)","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.thetimes.com/culture/theatre-dance/article/woman-in-mind-review-sheridan-smith-romesh-ranganathan-g6fmpjt7x?gaa_at=eafs&gaa_n=AWEtsqcIcldqAzyX1r8EjNKOERNAMxhYlntO4A56-TejZgN_dL59iFcauE5-uiJuCug%3D&gaa_ts=695e2bfd&gaa_sig=YLaLrMFfRfo6Z2QmT","d":"2026-01-07","q":"It’s so cheering to see the West End can still take risks, and even more encouraging to know that Smith and co will be taking the play out of London, albeit briefly, after the run finishes."},{"cn":"Arifa Akbar","o":"The Guardian","s":78,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.theguardian.com/stage/2026/jan/06/woman-in-mind-review-revival-that-stands-test-of-time-for-its-originality","d":"2026-01-06","q":"Smith plays the part with whimsical daintiness and subtlety, throwing out mischievous or slighted looks."},{"cn":"Nick Curtis","o":"Evening Standard","s":63,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.standard.co.uk/culture/theatre/woman-in-mind-duke-of-york-s-theatre-review-b1265306.html","d":"2026-01-07","q":"It's done with Ayckbourn's typical fluency, but concept overwhelms character: everyone, including Susan, is thinly drawn."},{"cn":"Olivia Rook","o":"London Theatre","s":83,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.londontheatre.co.uk/reviews/woman-in-mind-review-sheridan-smith-romesh-ranganathan","d":"2026-01-07","q":"This revival of Woman in Mind is gripping and deeply resonant."},{"cn":"Sarah Crompton","o":"WhatsOnStage","s":66,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.whatsonstage.com/news/woman-in-mind-west-end-review-sheridan-smith-gives-a-strong-turn-in-an-outdated-tragicomedy_1707895/","d":"2026-01-07","q":"It's a lovely, naturalistic performance, but it exposes the artificiality of the play."},{"cn":"Alice Saville","o":"The Independent","s":64,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/theatre-dance/reviews/woman-in-mind-sheridan-smith-romesh-ranganathan-b2895867.html","d":"2026-01-07","q":"Smith can't do much to disguise the fact that this is frivolous fare, unlikely to become a set text for students of either contemporary theatre or psychology."},{"cn":"Andrzej Lukowski","o":"Time Out London","s":63,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.timeout.com/london/theatre/woman-in-mind-review","d":"2026-01-07","q":"But it never really takes the time to slow down and properly explore loneliness, middle aged sexuality, or even mental health."},{"cn":"Sam Marlowe","o":"The Stage","s":61,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.thestage.co.uk/reviews/woman-in-mind-review-duke-of-yorks-theatre-london-sheridan-smith-alan-ayckbourn-michael-longhurst","d":"2026-01-07","q":"Four decades on from its premiere, the play sometimes still startles, but in the end it simply doesn’t cut it."}],"au":{"score":69,"designation":"Shrugging","sources":{"mz":{"s":69,"c":117,"sr":3.4}}},"hi":"https://images.ctfassets.net/6pezt69ih962/2qicnXO2vAo4DyTOD15BR8/3edebf102ae33fa7ff9553d62a0d6011/8458_12_WIM_TT_1440x580px.png","ca":[{"n":"Sheridan Smith","r":"Susan"},{"n":"Romesh Ranganathan","r":"Bill"},{"n":"Louise Brealey","r":"Muriel"},{"n":"Tim McMullan","r":"Gerald"},{"n":"Sule Rimi","r":"Andy"},{"n":"Chris Jenks","r":"Tony"},{"n":"Safia Oakley-Green","r":"Lucy"},{"n":"Taylor Uttley","r":"Rick"}]}